  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For I say, through the grace given unto me, to every man that is among you, not to think of himself more highly than he ought to think; but to think soberly, according as God hath dealt to every man the measure of faith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For as we have many members in one body, and all members have not the same office:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "So we, being many, are one body in Christ, and every one members one of another.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, whether prophecy, let us prophesy according to the proportion of faith;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Or ministry, let us wait on our ministering: or he that teacheth, on teaching;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Or he that exhorteth, on exhortation: he that giveth, let him do it with simplicity; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Let love be without dissimulation. Abhor that which is evil; cleave to that which is good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Be kindly affectioned one to another with brotherly love; in honour preferring one another;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Not slothful in business; fervent in spirit; serving the Lord;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Distributing to the necessity of saints; given to hospitality.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Bless them which persecute you: bless, and curse not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Be of the same mind one toward another. Mind not high things, but condescend to men of low estate. Be not wise in your own conceits.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Recompense to no man evil for evil. Provide things honest in the sight of all men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Therefore if thine enemy hunger, feed him; if he thirst, give him drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire on his head.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:12:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 12:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:12:21"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
